    "answer_text": "Given that, ∠ABC = ∠FED (1), ∠BAC = ∠EFD (2). The two angles of ΔABC are equal to the two respective angles of ΔFED. Also, the sum of all interior angles of a triangle is 180º. Therefore, the third angle of both triangles will also be equal in measure, ∠BCA = ∠EDF (3). Also, given that, BC = ED (4). By using equations (1), (3), and (4), we obtain ΔABC ≅ ΔFED (ASA criterion).",
    "answer_latex": null,
